---
const methods = [
  { name: 'Pomodoro', summary: '25 on, 5 off. Every fourth break is 15.' },
  {
    name: '52/17',
    summary: 'The rhythm DeskTime found in its most productive users.',
  },
  {
    name: '112/26',
    summary: 'The longer sprints they found once remote work was normal.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section wrap methods" aria-labelledby="methods-title">
  <div data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow">Optional</p>
    <h2 id="methods-title">
      Prefer working in blocks? It is there if you want it.
    </h2>
    <p>
      Off by default, because the plain timer is the point. Turn on a method in
      Settings and a band across the middle fills as the block runs. When it
      ends you get a notification and the other side glows, ready for a tap.
      Switching early asks for a second tap, so a stray touch never cuts a block
      short.
    </p>
    <ul class="method-chips">
      {methods.map((method) => (
        <li>
          <strong>{method.name}</strong> · {method.summary}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="methods-demo" data-reveal aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="md-half is-top">
      <div class="md-time">18:11</div>
      <div class="md-label">Studying</div>
      <div class="md-caption">7 min left</div>
      <div class="md-dots">
        <i class="is-done"></i>
        <i class="is-done"></i>
        <i class="is-live"></i>
        <i></i>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="md-half is-bottom">
      <div class="md-time">10:00</div>
      <div class="md-label">Procrastinating</div>
      <div class="md-caption"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="md-band"></div>
  </div>
</section>
